/* Verse Games: THE WHOLE COUNSEL - Exodus chapters 26-30
   Verse text is filled/verified from the KJV by tools/fill-verses.js */
VG.registerBibleChapters("exodus", [
{n:26, name:"The Tabernacle", seal:{ref:"Exodus 26:1",verse:"Moreover thou shalt make the tabernacle with ten curtains of fine twined linen, and blue, and purple, and scarlet: with cherubims of cunning work shalt thou make them."}, facts:["Did you know the innermost curtains wove cherubim right into the fabric, so the dwelling place of God was surrounded by images of His heavenly guard? (Exodus 26:1)","Did you know the standing boards were ten cubits tall, joined by forty silver sockets on each long side, showing that the meeting place of God was built strong and true? (Exodus 26:16-19)","Did you know the veil that separated the Holy Place from the Most Holy was woven with the same blue, purple, and scarlet as the outer coverings, beauty marking the way into God's presence? (Exodus 26:31)"], questions:[
{q:"How many curtains formed the inner covering of the tabernacle?", options:["Ten","Eleven","Twelve","Seven"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 26:1",verse:"Moreover thou shalt make the tabernacle with ten curtains of fine twined linen, and blue, and purple, and scarlet: with cherubims of cunning work shalt thou make them.", insight:"God's dwelling began with a counted, careful design. Nothing in His house was random, and His people were meant to see His order in every thread."},
{q:"Of what was the hanging for the door of the tent made?", options:["Blue, purple, scarlet, and fine twined linen","Goats' hair and rams' skins dyed red","Pure gold overlaid with silver","Acacia wood covered with brass"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 26:36",verse:"And thou shalt make an hanging for the door of the tent, of blue, and purple, and scarlet, and fine twined linen, wrought with needlework.", insight:"Even the doorway of God's house was woven with color and beauty. Every entrance into His presence was made glorious."},
{q:"How long was each of the ten curtains?", options:["Twenty-eight cubits","Thirty cubits","Twenty cubits","Twenty-five cubits"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 26:2",verse:"The length of one curtain shall be eight and twenty cubits, and the breadth of one curtain four cubits: and every one of the curtains shall have one measure.", insight:"Every curtain was cut to the exact same measure. God's precision in small details teaches us that He notices and cares about everything in our lives too."},
{q:"How wide was each of the ten curtains?", options:["Four cubits","Five cubits","Three cubits","Six cubits"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 26:2",verse:"The length of one curtain shall be eight and twenty cubits, and the breadth of one curtain four cubits: and every one of the curtains shall have one measure.", insight:"Length and breadth were both appointed by God. His plans are complete in every direction, lacking nothing and needing nothing added."},
{q:"How were the curtains joined together?", options:["Five by five","Ten in a single row","Three by three","All eleven together"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 26:3",verse:"The five curtains shall be coupled together one to another; and other five curtains shall be coupled one to another.", insight:"The curtains were coupled into two great sets, separate pieces made one. God delights to join His people together into one dwelling for Himself."},
{q:"What color were the loops fastened to the edge of the outermost curtain?", options:["Blue","Scarlet","Gold","Purple"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 26:4",verse:"And thou shalt make loops of blue upon the edge of the one curtain from the selvedge in the coupling; and likewise shalt thou make in the uttermost edge of another curtain, in the coupling of the second.", insight:"Even the small loops that held the curtains were colored blue, a heavenly hue. No part of serving God is too small to be touched with beauty."},
{q:"How many loops were placed on the edge of each set of curtains?", options:["Fifty","Forty","Thirty","Sixty"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 26:5",verse:"Fifty loops shalt thou make in the one curtain, and fifty loops shalt thou make in the edge of the curtain that is in the coupling of the second; that the loops may take hold one of another.", insight:"Fifty loops faced fifty loops, each one matched to its fellow. Unity in God's house is not accidental; it is arranged with intention."},
{q:"With what were the linen curtains coupled into one tabernacle?", options:["Fifty taches of gold","Fifty taches of brass","Fifty taches of silver","Fifty cords of blue"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 26:6",verse:"And thou shalt make fifty taches of gold, and couple the curtains together with the taches: and it shall be one tabernacle.", insight:"Gold, the most precious metal, bound the holy curtains. What belongs to God is held together by what is costly, pointing to the precious blood of Christ."},
{q:"How many curtains of goats' hair lay above the linen curtains?", options:["Eleven","Ten","Twelve","Nine"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 26:7",verse:"And thou shalt make curtains of goats’ hair to be a covering upon the tabernacle: eleven curtains shalt thou make.", insight:"An extra curtain of rougher hair covered the fine linen, sheltering the beauty within. God protects what is precious, often with coverings we do not see."},
{q:"How long was each goats' hair curtain?", options:["Thirty cubits","Twenty-eight cubits","Twenty-five cubits","Thirty-five cubits"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 26:8",verse:"The length of one curtain shall be thirty cubits, and the breadth of one curtain four cubits: and the eleven curtains shall be all of one measure.", insight:"The outer curtains were longer than the inner, draping over and guarding them. God's covering over His people always extends a little further than we expect."},
{q:"What was done with the sixth goats' hair curtain?", options:["It was doubled in the forefront of the tabernacle","It was folded away beneath the others","It was cut into two equal parts","It was given to the priests for clothing"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 26:9",verse:"And thou shalt couple five curtains by themselves, and six curtains by themselves, and shalt double the sixth curtain in the forefront of the tabernacle.", insight:"The doubled curtain faced the entrance, greeting all who drew near. God arranges His house so that His welcome is the first thing we meet."},
{q:"The goats' hair curtains were coupled with taches of what metal?", options:["Brass","Gold","Silver","Iron"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 26:11",verse:"And thou shalt make fifty taches of brass, and put the taches into the loops, and couple the tent together, that it may be one.", insight:"Brass, strong and enduring, joined the outer tent. God builds with strength where the weather of life beats hardest against His house."},
{q:"What covering was laid over the goats' hair curtains?", options:["Rams' skins dyed red","Badgers' skins","Fine twined linen","Goats' skins"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 26:14",verse:"And thou shalt make a covering for the tent of rams’ skins dyed red, and a covering above of badgers skins.", insight:"Red-dyed skins covered the tent, a splash of color against the wilderness. Even the roof of God's house spoke of sacrifice, the red reminding of blood shed for sin."},
{q:"What was the outermost covering of the tabernacle?", options:["Badgers' skins","Rams' skins dyed red","Blue cloth","Purple linen"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 26:14",verse:"And thou shalt make a covering for the tent of rams’ skins dyed red, and a covering above of badgers skins.", insight:"The plain outer skin hid glorious beauty within. Do not judge by appearances; God's greatest treasures are often wrapped in humble coverings."},
{q:"Of what wood were the standing boards of the tabernacle made?", options:["Shittim wood","Cedar wood","Fir wood","Olive wood"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 26:15",verse:"And thou shalt make boards for the tabernacle of shittim wood standing up.", insight:"Common desert wood, overlaid with gold, became the walls of God's house. God takes ordinary people and covers them with His glory."},
{q:"How tall was each standing board?", options:["Ten cubits","Eight cubits","Twelve cubits","Five cubits"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 26:16",verse:"Ten cubits shall be the length of a board, and a cubit and a half shall be the breadth of one board.", insight:"Ten cubits high stood every board, steady and upright. God calls His people to stand tall and firm in the faith, rooted in His foundation."},
{q:"How many boards stood along the south side of the tabernacle?", options:["Twenty","Ten","Six","Forty"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 26:18",verse:"And thou shalt make the boards for the tabernacle, twenty boards on the south side southward.", insight:"Twenty boards on each long side gave the house its length. There is room in God's dwelling for all His people, side by side."},
{q:"How many silver sockets held the twenty boards on the south side?", options:["Forty","Twenty","Eighty","Thirty"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 26:19",verse:"And thou shalt make forty sockets of silver under the twenty boards; two sockets under one board for his two tenons, and two sockets under another board for his two tenons.", insight:"Two silver sockets under every board anchored it to the ground. Silver speaks of redemption; we stand firm only because we have been bought with a price."},
{q:"What three colors ran through the veil of the tabernacle?", options:["Blue, purple, and scarlet","Red, gold, and green","White, black, and gray","Yellow, orange, and brown"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 26:31",verse:"And thou shalt make a vail of blue, and purple, and scarlet, and fine twined linen of cunning work: with cherubims shall it be made:", insight:"The veil wore royal colors, for behind it sat the throne of the King. Beauty itself guarded the entrance to the Most Holy Place."},
{q:"What did the veil divide?", options:["The holy place from the most holy","The court from the tabernacle","The camp from the sanctuary","The altar from the laver"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 26:33",verse:"And thou shalt hang up the vail under the taches, that thou mayest bring in thither within the vail the ark of the testimony: and the vail shall divide unto you between the holy place and the most holy.", insight:"The veil marked how holy God is and how far sin separates us. One day it would tear at the cross, and the way into God's presence would stand open."}
]},
{n:27, name:"The Altar and the Court", seal:{ref:"Exodus 27:20",verse:"And thou shalt command the children of Israel, that they bring thee pure oil olive beaten for the light, to cause the lamp to burn always."}, facts:["Did you know the bronze altar's four horns, made of the same wood as the altar itself, were the places where the blood of atonement was applied? (Exodus 27:2)","Did you know the lamp inside was to burn always, fed by pure beaten olive oil, a picture of worship that never goes out? (Exodus 27:20)","Did you know the court stretched a hundred cubits long, walled with fine linen on twenty pillars a side, so Israel could draw near yet stop short of the sanctuary itself? (Exodus 27:9-10)"], questions:[
{q:"Of what wood was the altar of burnt offering made?", options:["Shittim wood","Cedar wood","Olive wood","Fir wood"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 27:1",verse:"And thou shalt make an altar of shittim wood, five cubits long, and five cubits broad; the altar shall be foursquare: and the height thereof shall be three cubits.", insight:"The altar of sacrifice was made of the same humble desert wood as the tabernacle walls. God meets us with common things made holy by His purpose."},
{q:"How large was the altar, being square?", options:["Five cubits by five cubits","Three cubits by three cubits","Seven cubits by seven cubits","Ten cubits by ten cubits"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 27:1",verse:"And thou shalt make an altar of shittim wood, five cubits long, and five cubits broad; the altar shall be foursquare: and the height thereof shall be three cubits.", insight:"A perfect square, equal on every side. God's justice and mercy are perfectly balanced at the place where sin is dealt with."},
{q:"Of what metal were all the pins of the tabernacle and the court?", options:["Brass","Gold","Silver","Iron"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 27:19",verse:"All the vessels of the tabernacle in all the service thereof, and all the pins thereof, and all the pins of the court, shall be of brass.", insight:"Even the humble tent pins were brass, strong and appointed. In God's house, the smallest fastenings matter, and every servant has a place that holds."},
{q:"How many horns did the altar have?", options:["Four","Two","One","Six"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 27:2",verse:"And thou shalt make the horns of it upon the four corners thereof: his horns shall be of the same: and thou shalt overlay it with brass.", insight:"Four horns reached toward the four corners of the earth. God's power to save stretches to every direction, to all who will come."},
{q:"With what metal was the altar overlaid?", options:["Brass","Gold","Silver","Iron"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 27:2",verse:"And thou shalt make the horns of it upon the four corners thereof: his horns shall be of the same: and thou shalt overlay it with brass.", insight:"Brass endures fire, and the altar faced fire every day. God gives His servants strength that can stand the heat of testing."},
{q:"Of what metal were the altar's pans, shovels, basins, fleshhooks, and firepans made?", options:["Brass","Gold","Silver","Bronze and iron"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 27:3",verse:"And thou shalt make his pans to receive his ashes, and his shovels, and his basons, and his fleshhooks, and his firepans: all the vessels thereof thou shalt make of brass.", insight:"Every tool of the altar, down to the smallest pan, was brass. In God's service, no task is too lowly to be made with care and holiness."},
{q:"What kind of grate was set within the altar?", options:["A grate of brass network","A grate of iron bars","A grate of golden lattice","A grate of woven cords"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 27:4",verse:"And thou shalt make for it a grate of network of brass; and upon the net shalt thou make four brasen rings in the four corners thereof.", insight:"The network grate held the sacrifice over the fire. God provides the very structure by which our offerings are received."},
{q:"How was the altar constructed?", options:["Hollow with boards","Solid with stone","Filled with earth","Carved from one rock"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 27:8",verse:"Hollow with boards shalt thou make it: as it was shewed thee in the mount, so shall they make it.", insight:"Hollow with boards, the altar was light enough to carry through the wilderness. God's provision travels with His people wherever they go."},
{q:"How long were the hangings on the south side of the court?", options:["A hundred cubits","Fifty cubits","Seventy cubits","Thirty cubits"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 27:9",verse:"And thou shalt make the court of the tabernacle: for the south side southward there shall be hangings for the court of fine twined linen of an hundred cubits long for one side:", insight:"A hundred cubits of fine linen marked the boundary of the court. God sets holy boundaries, and within them His people find safety."},
{q:"Of what were the court's hangings made?", options:["Fine twined linen","Goats' hair","Blue wool","Scarlet cloth"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 27:9",verse:"And thou shalt make the court of the tabernacle: for the south side southward there shall be hangings for the court of fine twined linen of an hundred cubits long for one side:", insight:"White linen enclosed the court, a picture of purity. Drawing near to God means leaving the dust of the world outside the fence."},
{q:"How many pillars stood along the south side of the court?", options:["Twenty","Ten","Twelve","Forty"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 27:10",verse:"And the twenty pillars thereof and their twenty sockets shall be of brass; the hooks of the pillars and their fillets shall be of silver.", insight:"Twenty pillars upheld the linen wall on each long side. God's house stands firm because every part bears its share of the weight."},
{q:"Of what metal were the sockets of the court's pillars?", options:["Brass","Gold","Silver","Wood"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 27:10",verse:"And the twenty pillars thereof and their twenty sockets shall be of brass; the hooks of the pillars and their fillets shall be of silver.", insight:"Brass sockets grounded the pillars in the sand. Judgment begins at God's house, and brass reminds us that He is holy."},
{q:"Of what metal were the hooks of the pillars?", options:["Silver","Gold","Brass","Iron"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 27:17",verse:"All the pillars round about the court shall be filleted with silver; their hooks shall be of silver, and their sockets of brass.", insight:"Silver hooks held the linen to the pillars. Redemption, pictured in silver, is what binds God's people to His dwelling."},
{q:"How wide were the hangings on the west side of the court?", options:["Fifty cubits","A hundred cubits","Twenty cubits","Fifteen cubits"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 27:12",verse:"And for the breadth of the court on the west side shall be hangings of fifty cubits: their pillars ten, and their sockets ten.", insight:"Fifty cubits closed the back of the court. God's house is complete on every side; there is no gap in His protection."},
{q:"How wide was the gate of the court on the east?", options:["Twenty cubits","Fifteen cubits","Ten cubits","Fifty cubits"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 27:16",verse:"And for the gate of the court shall be an hanging of twenty cubits, of blue, and purple, and scarlet, and fine twined linen, wrought with needlework: and their pillars shall be four, and their sockets four.", insight:"A wide gate of embroidered blue, purple, and scarlet welcomed worshippers. The way to God is open and beautiful, and all may enter by sacrifice."},
{q:"How many pillars upheld the gate of the court?", options:["Four","Three","Five","Six"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 27:16",verse:"And for the gate of the court shall be an hanging of twenty cubits, of blue, and purple, and scarlet, and fine twined linen, wrought with needlework: and their pillars shall be four, and their sockets four.", insight:"Four pillars framed the entrance, steady and sure. Christ is the door, and the way in is plain, firm, and open to all."},
{q:"How high were the hangings of the court?", options:["Five cubits","Three cubits","Seven cubits","Ten cubits"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 27:18",verse:"The length of the court shall be an hundred cubits, and the breadth fifty every where, and the height five cubits of fine twined linen, and their sockets of brass.", insight:"Five cubits high, the linen wall stood above every eye. Holiness is set apart; it cannot be seen or reached by casual glances."},
{q:"How broad was the court from side to side?", options:["Fifty cubits","A hundred cubits","Thirty cubits","Twenty cubits"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 27:18",verse:"The length of the court shall be an hundred cubits, and the breadth fifty every where, and the height five cubits of fine twined linen, and their sockets of brass.", insight:"Fifty by a hundred cubits gave room for the whole nation to gather. God's house has space for multitudes; none who come are turned away."},
{q:"What kind of oil was commanded for the light?", options:["Pure oil olive beaten","Pressed oil of myrrh","Mixed oil of spices","Oil of cedar"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 27:20",verse:"And thou shalt command the children of Israel, that they bring thee pure oil olive beaten for the light, to cause the lamp to burn always.", insight:"Beaten, not merely pressed, the oil came from olives crushed to give their best. The brightest light for God often comes from a pressed and yielded heart."},
{q:"Who was to order the lamp from evening to morning before the LORD?", options:["Aaron and his sons","Moses alone","The elders of Israel","The Levites in turn"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 27:21",verse:"In the tabernacle of the congregation without the vail, which is before the testimony, Aaron and his sons shall order it from evening to morning before the LORD: it shall be a statute for ever unto their generations on the behalf of the children of Israel.", insight:"The priests kept the flame night and day, a charge passed down forever. Faithfulness in small daily duties keeps the light of God burning bright."}
]},
{n:28, name:"The Priestly Garments", seal:{ref:"Exodus 28:2",verse:"And thou shalt make holy garments for Aaron thy brother for glory and for beauty."}, facts:["Did you know the high priest carried the names of all twelve tribes on his shoulders and over his heart, bearing the people before God whenever he ministered? (Exodus 28:12, 29)","Did you know the golden bells on the robe's hem rang as Aaron moved, and their sound was heard so that he would not die when entering God's presence? (Exodus 28:35)","Did you know a plate of pure gold on the mitre was engraved HOLINESS TO THE LORD and worn on Aaron's forehead as a constant reminder of consecration? (Exodus 28:36)"], questions:[
{q:"Who did God set apart to minister to Him in the priest's office?", options:["Aaron and his sons","Moses and Joshua","The elders of Israel","The tribe of Judah"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 28:1",verse:"And take thou unto thee Aaron thy brother, and his sons with him, from among the children of Israel, that he may minister unto me in the priest’s office, even Aaron, Nadab and Abihu, Eleazar and Ithamar, Aaron’s sons.", insight:"God chose Aaron's family for a holy calling. He still calls ordinary families into His service, setting them apart for His purposes."},
{q:"Which sons of Aaron were named for the priesthood?", options:["Nadab, Abihu, Eleazar, and Ithamar","Gershon, Kohath, and Merari","Hur, Caleb, and Nun","Joab, Abishai, and Asahel"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 28:1",verse:"And take thou unto thee Aaron thy brother, and his sons with him, from among the children of Israel, that he may minister unto me in the priest’s office, even Aaron, Nadab and Abihu, Eleazar and Ithamar, Aaron’s sons.", insight:"Each son was named, none forgotten. God knows His servants by name, and every calling in His house matters."},
{q:"For what two purposes were the holy garments made?", options:["For glory and for beauty","For warmth and for comfort","For battle and for travel","For mourning and for fasting"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 28:2",verse:"And thou shalt make holy garments for Aaron thy brother for glory and for beauty.", insight:"Glory and beauty, not mere usefulness, shaped the priest's clothing. Worship should be beautiful, because it reflects the glory of God Himself."},
{q:"Who was to make the garments?", options:["Men wise of heart, filled with the spirit of wisdom","The elders at the gate","Aaron and his sons alone","The craftsmen of Egypt"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 28:3",verse:"And thou shalt speak unto all that are wise hearted, whom I have filled with the spirit of wisdom, that they may make Aaron’s garments to consecrate him, that he may minister unto me in the priest’s office.", insight:"God filled craftsmen with His Spirit for needlework. Every skill, even sewing and engraving, becomes sacred when offered to Him."},
{q:"Of what materials was the ephod made?", options:["Gold, blue, purple, scarlet, and fine linen","Silver, white, crimson, and wool","Brass, blue, green, and linen","Gold, black, and goats' hair"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 28:5",verse:"And they shall take gold, and blue, and purple, and scarlet, and fine linen.", insight:"Gold and rich colors wove through the ephod. God weaves many gifts and graces together in the life of everyone who serves Him."},
{q:"What stones were set on the shoulderpieces of the ephod?", options:["Onyx stones","Emerald stones","Ruby stones","Topaz stones"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 28:9",verse:"And thou shalt take two onyx stones, and grave on them the names of the children of Israel:", insight:"Precious onyx bore the names of God's people. Those who serve God carry His people with them, precious in His sight."},
{q:"What was engraved on the two shoulder stones?", options:["The names of the children of Israel","The ten commandments","The name of the LORD","The twelve stars"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 28:9",verse:"And thou shalt take two onyx stones, and grave on them the names of the children of Israel:", insight:"The tribes' names were carved into stone, not written in sand. God's people are permanently engraved on His heart and on His servant's shoulders."},
{q:"How were the twelve names divided between the two stones?", options:["Six on one stone and six on the other, by birth order","Seven on one and five on the other","All twelve on each stone","Four on one and eight on the other"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 28:10",verse:"Six of their names on one stone, and the other six names of the rest on the other stone, according to their birth.", insight:"Six and six, in the order of their birth. God is orderly in how He remembers His people; none is first by accident and none is last by neglect."},
{q:"What were the engraved shoulder stones called?", options:["Stones of memorial","Stones of judgment","Stones of witness","Stones of the covenant"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 28:12",verse:"And thou shalt put the two stones upon the shoulders of the ephod for stones of memorial unto the children of Israel: and Aaron shall bear their names before the LORD upon his two shoulders for a memorial.", insight:"A memorial before the LORD, the stones kept Israel in remembrance. God never forgets His people, and His servants must not forget them either."},
{q:"What was the name of the pouch worn on the ephod?", options:["The breastplate of judgment","The girdle of righteousness","The pouch of testimony","The bag of the covenant"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 28:15",verse:"And thou shalt make the breastplate of judgment with cunning work; after the work of the ephod thou shalt make it; of gold, of blue, and of purple, and of scarlet, and of fine twined linen, shalt thou make it.", insight:"Judgment rested over the priest's heart, for God's decisions flow from His love. True judgment is never cold; it is carried close to the heart."},
{q:"What stones formed the first row of the breastplate?", options:["Sardius, topaz, and carbuncle","Emerald, sapphire, and diamond","Ligure, agate, and amethyst","Beryl, onyx, and jasper"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 28:17",verse:"And thou shalt set in it settings of stones, even four rows of stones: the first row shall be a sardius, a topaz, and a carbuncle: this shall be the first row.", insight:"Each stone was set with care in its row. God places every believer exactly where He wills in the body, each one shining in its own color."},
{q:"What stones formed the second row of the breastplate?", options:["Emerald, sapphire, and diamond","Sardius, topaz, and carbuncle","Ligure, agate, and amethyst","Beryl, onyx, and jasper"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 28:18",verse:"And the second row shall be an emerald, a sapphire, and a diamond.", insight:"Row by row the breastplate grew in splendor. Spiritual beauty is built stone by stone, grace upon grace, over a lifetime."},
{q:"What stones formed the third row of the breastplate?", options:["Ligure, agate, and amethyst","Sardius, topaz, and carbuncle","Emerald, sapphire, and diamond","Beryl, onyx, and jasper"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 28:19",verse:"And the third row a ligure, an agate, and an amethyst.", insight:"No two rows were alike, yet all were one breastplate. God's people differ in gift and calling, but together they form one beautiful whole."},
{q:"What stones formed the fourth row of the breastplate?", options:["Beryl, onyx, and jasper","Sardius, topaz, and carbuncle","Emerald, sapphire, and diamond","Ligure, agate, and amethyst"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 28:20",verse:"And the fourth row a beryl, and an onyx, and a jasper: they shall be set in gold in their inclosings.", insight:"Twelve stones in four rows completed the work. God finishes what He starts, and His design for His people lacks nothing."},
{q:"What did the twelve stones on the breastplate represent?", options:["The twelve tribes of Israel","The twelve months of the year","The twelve apostles","The twelve gates of heaven"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 28:21",verse:"And the stones shall be with the names of the children of Israel, twelve, according to their names, like the engravings of a signet; every one with his name shall they be according to the twelve tribes.", insight:"Every tribe had its stone, none missing. In God's family there are no forgotten members; each one is counted and cherished."},
{q:"What two mysterious objects were placed in the breastplate?", options:["The Urim and the Thummim","The rod and the staff","The seal and the signet","The scroll and the lamp"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 28:30",verse:"And thou shalt put in the breastplate of judgment the Urim and the Thummim; and they shall be upon Aaron’s heart, when he goeth in before the LORD: and Aaron shall bear the judgment of the children of Israel upon his heart before the LORD continually.", insight:"Urim and Thummim guided God's decisions for His people. When we carry God's word over our hearts, we walk in His counsel and not our own."},
{q:"Of what color was the robe of the ephod?", options:["All of blue","All of scarlet","All of purple","All of white"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 28:31",verse:"And thou shalt make the robe of the ephod all of blue.", insight:"A robe all of blue wrapped the priest, the color of heaven. Those who serve God should carry the atmosphere of heaven with them."},
{q:"What hung around the hem of the blue robe?", options:["Pomegranates and golden bells","Tassels and silver coins","Ribbons and braided cords","Linen strips and beads"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 28:33",verse:"And beneath upon the hem of it thou shalt make pomegranates of blue, and of purple, and of scarlet, round about the hem thereof; and bells of gold between them round about:", insight:"Fruitfulness and music ringed the robe's hem, pomegranates for fruit and bells for sound. A life near God should bear fruit and make a joyful sound."},
{q:"Why was the sound of the bells to be heard when Aaron entered the holy place?", options:["That he die not","That the people would sing","That the lamps would stay lit","That the veil would open"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 28:35",verse:"And it shall be upon Aaron to minister: and his sound shall be heard when he goeth in unto the holy place before the LORD, and when he cometh out, that he die not.", insight:"The bells testified that the priest still lived and moved before God. Our walk with God should be heard in a life that keeps moving in obedience."},
{q:"What words were engraved on the golden plate of the mitre?", options:["HOLINESS TO THE LORD","GLORY TO GOD ON HIGH","THE LORD IS MY SHEPHERD","BLESSED BE HIS NAME"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 28:36",verse:"And thou shalt make a plate of pure gold, and grave upon it, like the engravings of a signet, HOLINESS TO THE LORD.", insight:"Holiness to the LORD crowned the priest's forehead, where all could see. A consecrated mind, set apart for God, is the believer's highest ornament."}
]},
{n:29, name:"Consecrating the Priests", seal:{ref:"Exodus 29:45",verse:"And I will dwell among the children of Israel, and will be their God."}, facts:["Did you know the consecration blood was placed on the right ear, the right thumb, and the right great toe, marking the priest's hearing, work, and walk as holy? (Exodus 29:20)","Did you know two lambs were offered every day, morning and evening, for generations, a continual reminder that fellowship with God never rests? (Exodus 29:38)","Did you know God states the purpose of it all plainly: that He might dwell among the children of Israel and be their God? (Exodus 29:45)"], questions:[
{q:"What animals were taken for the consecration of Aaron and his sons?", options:["One young bullock and two rams without blemish","Two bullocks and one ram","Seven lambs and a goat","A bullock and seven rams"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 29:1",verse:"And this is the thing that thou shalt do unto them to hallow them, to minister unto me in the priest’s office: Take one young bullock, and two rams without blemish,", insight:"Spotless animals, without blemish, were required. God deserves the best we have, and the perfect sacrifice pointed to Christ, the Lamb without spot."},
{q:"What kind of bread was brought for the consecration?", options:["Unleavened bread","Leavened loaves","Honey cakes","Barley bread"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 29:2",verse:"And unleavened bread, and cakes unleavened tempered with oil, and wafers unleavened anointed with oil: of wheaten flour shalt thou make them.", insight:"No leaven, the picture of sin, was allowed in the offering. Coming to God means leaving sin behind, not mixing it into our worship."},
{q:"Where were Aaron and his sons washed with water?", options:["At the door of the tabernacle","At the laver in the court","At the river of Egypt","At the altar of brass"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 29:4",verse:"And Aaron and his sons thou shalt bring unto the door of the tabernacle of the congregation, and shalt wash them with water.", insight:"Washing came before clothing and anointing. Cleansing always comes first in God's order; we are washed before we are clothed in His service."},
{q:"How was Aaron anointed?", options:["The anointing oil was poured on his head","Oil was sprinkled on his feet","His hands were dipped in oil","Oil was burned as incense"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 29:7",verse:"Then shalt thou take the anointing oil, and pour it upon his head, and anoint him.", insight:"Oil poured on the head set Aaron apart for God. The Holy Spirit still anoints believers today, marking them for God's work."},
{q:"What kind of statute was the priest's office to be?", options:["A perpetual statute","A temporary custom","A yearly festival","A tribal tradition"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 29:9",verse:"And thou shalt gird them with girdles, Aaron and his sons, and put the bonnets on them: and the priest’s office shall be theirs for a perpetual statute: and thou shalt consecrate Aaron and his sons.", insight:"Perpetual, never ending, was the priesthood. God's call on a life is not for a season; it is forever."},
{q:"What did Aaron and his sons do before the bullock was killed?", options:["They laid their hands on its head","They washed its feet","They tied it to the altar","They anointed it with oil"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 29:10",verse:"And thou shalt cause a bullock to be brought before the tabernacle of the congregation: and Aaron and his sons shall put their hands upon the head of the bullock.", insight:"Laying on hands identified the offerer with the offering. Our sins were laid on Christ when He became our sacrifice."},
{q:"Where was the blood of the bullock put?", options:["On the horns of the altar","On the veil of the temple","On the doorposts","On the mercy seat"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 29:12",verse:"And thou shalt take of the blood of the bullock, and put it upon the horns of the altar with thy finger, and pour all the blood beside the bottom of the altar.", insight:"Blood on the horns spoke of power and atonement. The blood of Jesus still speaks for us, with power to cleanse every sin."},
{q:"What was done with the flesh of the sin offering?", options:["It was burned outside the camp","It was eaten by the priests","It was buried in the court","It was given to the poor"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 29:14",verse:"But the flesh of the bullock, and his skin, and his dung, shalt thou burn with fire without the camp: it is a sin offering.", insight:"The sin offering was carried outside, away from the camp. Christ also suffered outside the gate, bearing our shame so we could be brought near."},
{q:"How was the first ram offered?", options:["It was burned wholly on the altar as a sweet savour","It was divided among the priests","Its blood was poured on the ground","It was set free in the wilderness"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 29:18",verse:"And thou shalt burn the whole ram upon the altar: it is a burnt offering unto the LORD: it is a sweet savour, an offering made by fire unto the LORD.", insight:"Wholly burned, nothing held back, the offering rose as a sweet savour. God loves a wholehearted surrender, with nothing kept in reserve."},
{q:"On which three parts of the body was the blood of the second ram placed?", options:["The right ear, the right thumb, and the right great toe","The forehead, the hands, and the feet","The left ear, the left thumb, and the left toe","The shoulders, the elbows, and the knees"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 29:20",verse:"Then shalt thou kill the ram, and take of his blood, and put it upon the tip of the right ear of Aaron, and upon the tip of the right ear of his sons, and upon the thumb of their right hand, and upon the great toe of their right foot, and sprinkle the blood upon the altar round about.", insight:"Ear, hand, and foot were marked: what we hear, what we do, and where we go all belong to God. Consecration touches the whole life."},
{q:"What was sprinkled on Aaron, his sons, and their garments?", options:["Blood and anointing oil","Water and ashes","Wine and flour","Milk and honey"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 29:21",verse:"And thou shalt take of the blood that is upon the altar, and of the anointing oil, and sprinkle it upon Aaron, and upon his garments, and upon his sons, and upon the garments of his sons with him: and he shall be hallowed, and his garments, and his sons, and his sons’ garments with him.", insight:"Blood and oil together sanctified the priests. Cleansing by the blood and filling by the Spirit still go together in the Christian life."},
{q:"What was the second ram called?", options:["The ram of consecration","The ram of atonement","The ram of the covenant","The ram of thanksgiving"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 29:22",verse:"Also thou shalt take of the ram the fat and the rump, and the fat that covereth the inwards, and the caul above the liver, and the two kidneys, and the fat that is upon them, and the right shoulder; for it is a ram of consecration:", insight:"Consecration means being set apart wholly for God. The ram's name declared its purpose: these men now belonged to the LORD alone."},
{q:"What part of the ram of consecration was waved as a wave offering?", options:["The breast","The shoulder","The thigh","The head"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 29:26",verse:"And thou shalt take the breast of the ram of Aaron’s consecration, and wave it for a wave offering before the LORD: and it shall be thy part.", insight:"The breast, over the heart, was lifted to God. Worship begins in the heart; God wants our affections waved before Him first."},
{q:"What was done with the holy garments after Aaron's death?", options:["They passed to his son who followed him as priest","They were buried with Aaron","They were burned on the altar","They were hung in the tabernacle"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 29:29",verse:"And the holy garments of Aaron shall be his sons’ after him, to be anointed therein, and to be consecrated in them.", insight:"The garments outlived the man, passing to the next priest. God's work continues beyond any one servant; the calling is greater than the person."},
{q:"How many days was Aaron's successor to wear the holy garments?", options:["Seven days","Three days","Forty days","One day"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 29:30",verse:"And that son that is priest in his stead shall put them on seven days, when he cometh into the tabernacle of the congregation to minister in the holy place.", insight:"Seven days of wearing marked a complete consecration. God takes time to prepare His servants; there are no shortcuts to holiness."},
{q:"How many days were Aaron and his sons to be consecrated?", options:["Seven days","Three days","Ten days","Forty days"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 29:35",verse:"And thus shalt thou do unto Aaron, and to his sons, according to all things which I have commanded thee: seven days shalt thou consecrate them.", insight:"A full week of consecration set them apart. Becoming God's servant is a complete work, not a hurried ceremony."},
{q:"How many lambs were offered day by day continually?", options:["Two","One","Seven","Four"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 29:38",verse:"Now this is that which thou shalt offer upon the altar; two lambs of the first year day by day continually.", insight:"Two lambs every day, without fail, for generations. God's mercies are new every morning, and His people respond with continual worship."},
{q:"When were the two daily lambs offered?", options:["One in the morning and the other at evening","Both at noon","Both at midnight","One at dawn and one at midnight"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 29:39",verse:"The one lamb thou shalt offer in the morning; and the other lamb thou shalt offer at even:", insight:"Morning and evening framed each day with sacrifice. Begin the day with God and end the day with God, and the hours between will be blessed."},
{q:"What was mingled with the tenth deal of flour in the daily offering?", options:["The fourth part of a hin of beaten oil","A hin of wine","Two handfuls of frankincense","A measure of honey"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 29:40",verse:"And with the one lamb a tenth deal of flour mingled with the fourth part of an hin of beaten oil; and the fourth part of an hin of wine for a drink offering.", insight:"Fine flour and beaten oil, the best of the field and the fruit of crushing. God receives our finest gifts, given from yielded hearts."},
{q:"What did God promise at the end of the consecration?", options:["I will dwell among the children of Israel","I will destroy their enemies at once","I will make them rulers of nations","I will give them rest from labor"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 29:45",verse:"And I will dwell among the children of Israel, and will be their God.", insight:"This is the goal of it all: God dwelling with His people. Every sacrifice, every garment, every ritual pointed to this, that God might live among us."}
]},
{n:30, name:"Incense and Atonement", seal:{ref:"Exodus 30:8",verse:"And when Aaron lighteth the lamps at even, he shall burn incense upon it, a perpetual incense before the LORD throughout your generations."}, facts:["Did you know every Israelite twenty years and older paid the same half shekel, rich and poor alike, showing that atonement costs all people the same? (Exodus 30:14-15)","Did you know the priests had to wash their hands and feet at the bronze laver before ministering, lest they die, because holiness demands cleansing? (Exodus 30:20)","Did you know the holy anointing oil and the sacred incense could never be copied for ordinary use; they belonged to the LORD alone? (Exodus 30:32, 37)"], questions:[
{q:"Of what wood was the altar of incense made?", options:["Shittim wood","Cedar wood","Olive wood","Acacia and fir"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 30:1",verse:"And thou shalt make an altar to burn incense upon: of shittim wood shalt thou make it.", insight:"The same humble wood as the tabernacle walls, yet overlaid with gold. God takes the ordinary and makes it a vessel for prayer."},
{q:"What were the dimensions of the altar of incense?", options:["A cubit square and two cubits high","Two cubits square and one high","Five cubits square and three high","Half a cubit square and one high"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 30:2",verse:"A cubit shall be the length thereof, and a cubit the breadth thereof; foursquare shall it be: and two cubits shall be the height thereof: the horns thereof shall be of the same.", insight:"Small beside the great altar of brass, yet set with gold. Prayer may seem small, but in God's sight it is precious."},
{q:"With what was the altar of incense overlaid?", options:["Pure gold, with a crown of gold","Brass, with a crown of silver","Silver, with rings of brass","Gold leaf on cedar"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 30:3",verse:"And thou shalt overlay it with pure gold, the top thereof, and the sides thereof round about, and the horns thereof; and thou shalt make unto it a crown of gold round about.", insight:"Pure gold crowned the altar of prayer. Our prayers, offered through Christ, are crowned with glory before the throne."},
{q:"How many rings of gold were made for the altar of incense?", options:["Two","Four","One","Six"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 30:4",verse:"And two golden rings shalt thou make to it under the crown of it, by the two corners thereof, upon the two sides of it shalt thou make it; and they shall be for places for the staves to bear it withal.", insight:"Rings and staves meant the altar traveled with Israel. Prayer goes with God's people everywhere; it is never left behind."},
{q:"Where was the altar of incense placed?", options:["Before the veil that is by the ark","Outside the court gate","Beside the bronze laver","At the door of the court"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 30:6",verse:"And thou shalt put it before the vail that is by the ark of the testimony, before the mercy seat that is over the testimony, where I will meet with thee.", insight:"Closest to the Most Holy Place stood the altar of prayer. Intercession brings us nearer to God's presence than anything else."},
{q:"How often did Aaron burn sweet incense on the golden altar?", options:["Every morning","Once a week","Every evening only","Once a year"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 30:7",verse:"And Aaron shall burn thereon sweet incense every morning: when he dresseth the lamps, he shall burn incense upon it.", insight:"Every morning the sweet smoke rose. Begin each day with prayer, and let its fragrance rise before God all day long."},
{q:"When else was incense burned, making it perpetual?", options:["At evening, when Aaron lit the lamps","At noon, when the sun was high","At midnight, in the dark","Only on the Sabbath"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 30:8",verse:"And when Aaron lighteth the lamps at even, he shall burn incense upon it, a perpetual incense before the LORD throughout your generations.", insight:"Morning and evening, incense never ceased. Perpetual prayer, unbroken communion, is the heartbeat of a life with God."},
{q:"What was forbidden on the altar of incense?", options:["Strange incense and burnt sacrifice","Sweet incense","Prayer and praise","Oil and wine"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 30:9",verse:"Ye shall offer no strange incense thereon, nor burnt sacrifice, nor meat offering; neither shall ye pour drink offering thereon.", insight:"No strange fire, no foreign mixture. Worship must be God's way, not ours; He defines what is acceptable in His presence."},
{q:"How often was atonement made on the horns of the golden altar?", options:["Once a year","Every month","Every Sabbath","Every morning"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 30:10",verse:"And Aaron shall make an atonement upon the horns of it once in a year with the blood of the sin offering of atonements: once in the year shall he make atonement upon it throughout your generations: it is most holy unto the LORD.", insight:"Once a year the horns were cleansed with blood. Even our prayers need atonement; Christ's blood covers our worship too."},
{q:"How much was each man to give as atonement money?", options:["Half a shekel","A full shekel","A tenth of a shekel","Two shekels"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 30:13",verse:"This they shall give, every one that passeth among them that are numbered, half a shekel after the shekel of the sanctuary: (a shekel is twenty gerahs:) an half shekel shall be the offering of the LORD.", insight:"A set price, a ransom for every soul. Christ paid the full ransom for us, and its value never changes."},
{q:"How many gerahs made the shekel of the sanctuary?", options:["Twenty","Ten","Twelve","Thirty"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 30:13",verse:"This they shall give, every one that passeth among them that are numbered, half a shekel after the shekel of the sanctuary: (a shekel is twenty gerahs:) an half shekel shall be the offering of the LORD.", insight:"God's measure was exact and unchanging. His standards do not shift with the times; His word is the fixed measure of truth."},
{q:"From what age was every man numbered to give the half shekel?", options:["Twenty years old and above","Thirty years old and above","Twelve years old and above","Forty years old and above"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 30:14",verse:"Every one that passeth among them that are numbered, from twenty years old and above, shall give an offering unto the LORD.", insight:"At twenty, a man took his place among the numbered. There comes a day when each of us must stand and be counted before God."},
{q:"How did the rich man's offering compare to the poor man's?", options:["The rich gave no more and the poor no less","The rich gave double","The poor gave half","Each gave according to his wealth"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 30:15",verse:"The rich shall not give more, and the poor shall not give less than half a shekel, when they give an offering unto the LORD, to make an atonement for your souls.", insight:"Rich and poor paid the same ransom. Before God, all souls are equal in worth and equal in need of redemption."},
{q:"Of what metal was the laver made?", options:["Brass","Gold","Silver","Iron"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 30:18",verse:"Thou shalt also make a laver of brass, and his foot also of brass, to wash withal: and thou shalt put it between the tabernacle of the congregation and the altar, and thou shalt put water therein.", insight:"A brass laver for washing, strong to endure. God's cleansing is thorough and lasting; He washes us completely."},
{q:"Where was the laver placed?", options:["Between the tabernacle and the altar","Inside the most holy place","Outside the court gate","Beside the table of showbread"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 30:18",verse:"Thou shalt also make a laver of brass, and his foot also of brass, to wash withal: and thou shalt put it between the tabernacle of the congregation and the altar, and thou shalt put water therein.", insight:"Between the altar and the tent, washing stood in the middle. Cleansing comes between sacrifice and service; we are washed to serve."},
{q:"Why were the priests to wash their hands and feet?", options:["That they die not","That they stay warm","That the people would see","That the water stay pure"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 30:20",verse:"When they go into the tabernacle of the congregation, they shall wash with water, that they die not; or when they come near to the altar to minister, to burn offering made by fire unto the LORD:", insight:"Wash, or die: so serious is approaching God. Holiness is not optional for those who minister; it is a matter of life and death."},
{q:"How much pure myrrh went into the holy anointing oil?", options:["Five hundred shekels","Two hundred and fifty shekels","A hundred shekels","A thousand shekels"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 30:23",verse:"Take thou also unto thee principal spices, of pure myrrh five hundred shekels, and of sweet cinnamon half so much, even two hundred and fifty shekels, and of sweet calamus two hundred and fifty shekels,", insight:"Myrrh, fragrant through crushing, flowed into the holy oil. The sweetest anointing often comes through suffering yielded to God."},
{q:"How much cassia and olive oil went into the holy anointing oil?", options:["Five hundred shekels of cassia and a hin of olive oil","Two hundred shekels of cassia and half a hin","A thousand shekels and two hins","Fifty shekels and a log of oil"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 30:24",verse:"And of cassia five hundred shekels, after the shekel of the sanctuary, and of oil olive an hin:", insight:"Measured exactly, the holy oil was compounded by God's recipe. The Spirit's anointing is not mixed by human invention but by divine order."},
{q:"On whom was the holy anointing oil never to be poured?", options:["On man's flesh for common use","On the priests' heads","On the tabernacle vessels","On Aaron's garments"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 30:32",verse:"Upon man’s flesh shall it not be poured, neither shall ye make any other like it, after the composition of it: it is holy, and it shall be holy unto you.", insight:"The holy oil was not for common use. What God sets apart must stay set apart; we dare not treat holy things as ordinary."},
{q:"What four sweet spices formed the sacred incense?", options:["Stacte, onycha, galbanum, and pure frankincense","Myrrh, cinnamon, calamus, and cassia","Balm, honey, spikenard, and saffron","Aloes, myrrh, cassia, and cinnamon"], a:0, ref:"Exodus 30:34",verse:"And the LORD said unto Moses, Take unto thee sweet spices, stacte, and onycha, and galbanum; these sweet spices with pure frankincense: of each shall there be a like weight:", insight:"Four spices, equal weights, tempered together into one holy perfume. Prayer blends many graces, confession, thanks, praise, and need, into one sweet offering."}
]}
]);
